  "@consentPrivacy": {
    "description": "THE CONSENT SENTENCE OF RECORD (owner decision 2026-08-09, decisions-log.md). States exactly what is NOT collected AND names the withdrawal route. The last clause is the one the PUBLISHED POLICY already makes — sites/nikatru/privacy.html: 'You can turn usage statistics off at any time in the app's Settings' — so the wording it replaced was the one that under-stated the policy, not the other way round. Kept honest by features/settings/settings_screen.dart, which assert-consent-withdrawal-surface.mjs pins. Consumed by app.dart's `_ConsentPrompt` — the inline scrim, which is the only consent surface the app mounts."
