  },
  "promoCardDismissA11y": "Dismiss this offer",
  "@promoCardDismissA11y": {
    "description": "What a screen reader announces for the card's icon-only close control. An icon-only control with no accessible name is a dismissal a user cannot perform, which turns a dismissible card into an undismissable one for exactly the people least able to work around it."
  },
  "legalAcceptTerms": "I am 18 or older, I agree to the Terms of Service, and I have read the Privacy Policy.",
  "@legalAcceptTerms": {
    "description": "Consumed by features/auth/legal_consent_fields.dart. The BLOCKING sign-up clickwrap (research/43), and since 2026-09-05 the 18+ ATTESTATION required by [ADR 068] as well - the tick is the affirmative act, so the age floor rides on the control that already blocks registration rather than on a line nobody has to touch. ONE COMPLETE SENTENCE, with the two document links rendered as separate controls beneath it rather than as spans inside it — a rich-text 'I agree to the [Terms] and [Privacy Policy]' fixes English word order and leaves a translator splicing links into the middle of a clause whose verb belongs at the end. The wording distinguishes AGREEING to the terms from having READ the notice, which is the legal difference between the two documents."
  },
  "legalMarketingOptIn": "Email me occasional product news and offers. You can unsubscribe at any time.",
  "@legalMarketingOptIn": {
